"id": "masculine",
"el": "Αρσενικά ουσιαστικά",
"title": "Masculine nouns",
"span": "A1–B1",
"blurb": "The masculine nouns in -ος, -ας, -ης and -ής/-άς/-ούς/-ές, with their stress shifts, their -δες plurals and their vocatives.",
"intro": [
{
"p": "Masculine nouns end in **-ος, -ας, -ης** or, in a smaller group, **-ής, -άς, -ούς, -ές, -έας**. The ending of the nominative singular predicts all the other forms, and the article confirms them."
},
{
"p": "A quick test: in the singular, masculine nouns drop the final **-ς** in the genitive (for -ας/-ης) or accusative (for all). That is why you hear **τον άντρα, του άντρα** but **ο άντρας**."
},
